{"G1136":{"id":"G1136","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1136","disambiguated_id":"G1136 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H1463H","headword":"Γώγ","transliteration":"Gōg","lexical_morphology":"N:N--L","gloss_en":"Gog","definition_en":"Γώγ, ὁ (Heb. גּוֹג), indecl., \n Gog, assoc. with Magog (q.v): Rev.20:8.†\n (AS)","source_line":1268}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Gogue","count":1}]},"G1137":{"id":"G1137","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1137","disambiguated_id":"G1137 =","unique_id":"G1137","headword":"γωνία","transliteration":"gōnia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"corner","definition_en":"γωνία, -ας, ἡ \n (γόνυ), [in LXX chiefly for פִּנָּה ;] \nan angle, a corner: Mat.6:5, Act.26:26; τ. τέσσαρας γ. τ. γῆς, Rev.7:1, 20:8; κεφαλὴ γνωνίας (רֹאשׁ פִּנָּה, Ps 117(118):22, LXX), Mat.21:42, Mrk.12:10, Luk.20:17, Act.4:11, 1Pe.2:7.†\n (AS)","source_line":1269}],"occurrence_count":9,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"esquina","count":5},{"gloss":"cantos","count":2},{"gloss":"esquinas","count":1},{"gloss":"canto","count":1}]},"G124":{"id":"G124","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0124","disambiguated_id":"G0124 = a Group member of","unique_id":"H4714G","headword":"Αἰγύπτιος","transliteration":"Aiguptios","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"Egyptian","definition_en":"Αἰγύπτιος, -α, ον,\n Egyptian: Act.7:22,24,28 21:38, Heb.11:29.†\n (AS)","source_line":221}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"egípcio","count":3},{"gloss":"egípcios","count":2}]},"G1464":{"id":"G1464","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1464","disambiguated_id":"G1464 =","unique_id":"G1464","headword":"ἐγκοπή","transliteration":"egkopē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"hindrance","definition_en":"ἐγκοπή, see: ἐνκ-.\n ἐν-κοπή (Rec. ἐγκ-, see: ἐν; T, ἐκκ-), -ῆς, ἡ (ἐγκόπτω) ; \n 1. an incision, a cutting, break. 2. Metaphorical, an interruption, a hindrance: 1Co.9:12.†\n (AS)","source_line":1596}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"impedimento","count":1}]},"G1849":{"id":"G1849","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1849","disambiguated_id":"G1849 =","unique_id":"G1849","headword":"ἐξουσία","transliteration":"exousia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"authority","definition_en":"ἐξουσία, -ας, ἡ \n (ἔξεστι), [in LXX: 4Ki.20:13, Psa.113 (114):2 135 (136)8, 9, Isa.39:2, Jer.28 (51):28 (מֶמְשָׁלָה), frequently in Da for Aram. שָׁלְטָן, etc., Wis.10:14, Sir.9:13, al. ;] \n __1. prop., liberty or power to act, freedom to exercise the inward force or faculty expressed by δύναμις (which see): 1Co.9:12; ἐ. ἔχειν, 2Th.3:9; id. before inf., Jhn.10:18, 1Co.9:4, 5; with genitive obj., Rom.9:21; before ἐπί, with accusative, Rev.22:14; περί, 1Co.7:37. \n __2. Later (cf. Milligan, Th., 114; MM, Exp., xiv), of the power of right, authority: Mat.21:33, Mrk.11:28, Luk.20:2; of Messianic authority, Mat.9:6, Mrk.2:10, al.; of apostolic authority, 2Co.10:8 13:10; of the authority of government: Mat.8:9 28:18, Ju 25, Rev.12:10, al.; esp. of judicial authority, Luk.20:20, Jhn.19:10, 11. \n __3. Meton., \n__(a) jurisdiction: Luk.23:7 (cf. 1Ma.6:11, Isa.39:2); \n __(b) a ruler or magistrate: Rom.13:1-3; pl., Luk.12:11, Rom.13:1, Tit.3:1; \n __(with) of supramundane powers (syn. with ἀρχή, δύναμις, θρόνος, κυριότης): 1Co.15:24, Eph.1:21 3:10, Col.2:10, 1Pe.3:22, al. (Cremer. 236). \n SYN.: see: δύναμις. (AS)","source_line":1990}],"occurrence_count":102,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"autoridade","count":47},{"gloss":"poder","count":39},{"gloss":"autoridades","count":7},{"gloss":"direito","count":5},{"gloss":"jurisdição","count":1},{"gloss":"liberdade","count":1},{"gloss":"poderes","count":1},{"gloss":"domínio","count":1}]},"G2246":{"id":"G2246","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2246","disambiguated_id":"G2246 =","unique_id":"G2246","headword":"ἥλιος","transliteration":"hēlios","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"sun","definition_en":"ἥλιος, -ου, ὁ \n [in LXX chiefly for שֶׁמֶשׁ ;] \nthe sun: with art. (El., § 46, 5), Mat.5:45 13:43 17:2 24:29, Mrk.1:32 4:6 13:24 16:2, Luk.4:40, Act.2:20\" (LXX) Act.26:13, Eph.4:26, Jas.1:11, Rev.1:16 6:12 8:12 9:2 10:1 12:1 16:8 19:17 21:23; βλέπειν τὸν ἥ., Act.13:11; οὐδὲ μὴ πέσῃ ἐπ᾽ αὐτοὺς ὁ ἥ., Rev.7:16; without art., Mat.13:6, Luk.21:25 23:45, Act.27:20, 1Co.15:41, Rev.7:2 16:12 22:5.†\n (AS)","source_line":2391}],"occurrence_count":32,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sol","count":32}]},"G2449":{"id":"G2449","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2449","disambiguated_id":"G2449 = the Greek of","unique_id":"H3063N","headword":"Ἰουδαία","transliteration":"Ioudaia","lexical_morphology":"N:N-F-L","gloss_en":"Judea","definition_en":"§ Judea, Judean, \"land of the Judahites\" \nJudea, the southern party of the country, below Samaria, Mt. 2:1, 5, 22; 3:1; metonymy the inhabitants of Judea","source_line":2606}],"occurrence_count":44,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Judeia","count":44}]},"G2475":{"id":"G2475","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2475","disambiguated_id":"G2475 = a Group member of","unique_id":"H3478","headword":"Ἰσραηλίτης","transliteration":"Israēlitēs","lexical_morphology":"N:N--PG","gloss_en":"Israelite","definition_en":"Ἰσραηλείτης\n (Rec. -λίτης), ου, ὁ [in LXX: Num.25:8 (יִשְׂרָאֵל), 3Ki.21:1 (יִזְרְעֵאלִי; Luc. Ἰεζραηλίτης), etc. ;] \nan Israelite, the name expressive of theocratic privilege (see: Ἑβραῖος): Rom.9:4 11:1, 2Co.11:22; ἀληθῶς Ἰ., Jhn.1:48; ἄνδρες Ἰ., Act.2:22 3:12 5:35 13:16 21:23.†\n (AS)","source_line":2641}],"occurrence_count":9,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"israelitas","count":7},{"gloss":"israelita","count":2}]},"G2915":{"id":"G2915","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2915","disambiguated_id":"G2915 =","unique_id":"G2915","headword":"κριθή","transliteration":"krithē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"barley","definition_en":"κριθή, -ῆς, ἡ \n [in LXX for שְׂעֹרָה ;] \nbarley: pl. (as usually in cl.), Rev.6:6.†\n (AS)","source_line":3110}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"cevada","count":1}]},"G3156":{"id":"G3156","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3156","disambiguated_id":"G3156 =","unique_id":"G3156","headword":"Ματθαῖος","transliteration":"Matthaios","lexical_morphology":"N:N-M-P","gloss_en":"Matthew","definition_en":"Μαθθαῖος (Rec. Ματθ-, see WH, App., 159; Bl., § 3, 11; on the Semitic form, see Dalman, Words, 51; Gr., 142), -ου, ὁ, \n Matthew: Mt title., Mat.9:9 10:3, Mrk.3:18, Luk.6:15, Act.1:13 (cf. Λευεί).†\n (AS)","source_line":3366}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Mateus","count":5}]},"G3663":{"id":"G3663","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3663","disambiguated_id":"G3663 =","unique_id":"G3663","headword":"ὁμοιοπαθής","transliteration":"homoiopathēs","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"like","definition_en":"ὁμοιοπαθής, -ές\n (ὅμοιος, πάσχω), [in LXX: Wis.7:3, 4Ma.12:13 * ;] \nof like feelings or affections: with dative, Act.14:15, Jas.5:17.†\n (AS)","source_line":3779}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sujeitos","count":1},{"gloss":"quanto","count":1}]},"G3903":{"id":"G3903","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3903","disambiguated_id":"G3903 =","unique_id":"G3903","headword":"παρασκευάζω","transliteration":"paraskeuazō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to prepare","definition_en":"παρα-σκευάζω \n [in LXX: Jer.50:42 (עָרַךְ), etc. ;] \nto prepare, make ready: absol. (sc. τ. δεῖπνον, etc.; of. Hdt., ix, 82, 2Ma.2:27), Act.10:10; mid., to prepare, make preparations: 1Co.14:8 (cf. Je, l.with); pass., 2Co.9:2-3.†\n (AS)","source_line":4021}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"preparando","count":1},{"gloss":"preparará","count":1},{"gloss":"pronta","count":1},{"gloss":"possais","count":1}]},"G4022":{"id":"G4022","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4022","disambiguated_id":"G4022 =","unique_id":"G4022","headword":"περιέρχομαι","transliteration":"perierchomai","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to go around","definition_en":"περι-έρχομαι \n [in LXX chiefly for סָבַב ;] \nto go about (as an itinerant): Act.19:13 28:13 (περιελόντες, WH, R, mg.), Heb.11:37; τ. οἰκίας, from house to house: 1Ti.5:13.†\n (AS)","source_line":4144}],"occurrence_count":3,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"exorcistas","count":1},{"gloss":"ociosas","count":1},{"gloss":"andaram","count":1}]},"G4092":{"id":"G4092","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4092","disambiguated_id":"G4092 =","unique_id":"G4092","headword":"πίμπρημι","transliteration":"pimprēmi","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to swell up","definition_en":"πίμπρημι\n (in cl. prose, rare in the simple form), [in LXX: Num.5:21-22, 27 (צָבֶה) * ;] \n__1. to blow, burn. \n __2. Later, to cause to swell; mid., of parts of the body, to become swollen (LXX) : Act.28:6 (cf. ἐμπίπρημι).†\n (AS)","source_line":4216}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"inchar","count":1}]},"G4467":{"id":"G4467","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4467","disambiguated_id":"G4467 =","unique_id":"G4467","headword":"ῥᾳδιούργημα","transliteration":"rhadiourgēma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"crime","definition_en":"ῥᾳδιούργημα, -τος, τό\n (ῥᾳδιουργέω, to act recklessly or wrongly) \n__1. a reckless act. \n __2. crime, villany: Act.18:14.†\n (AS)","source_line":4600}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"crime","count":1}]},"G4666":{"id":"G4666","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4666","disambiguated_id":"G4666 =","unique_id":"G4666","headword":"σμύρνα","transliteration":"smurna","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"myrrh","definition_en":"σμύρνα\n (in some MSS, ζμ-; see Bl., § 3, 9), -ης, ἡ, [in LXX for מֹר ;] \nmyrrh, a resinous gum used as an unguent and for em­balming: Mat.2:11, Jhn.19:39.†\n (AS)","source_line":4812}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"mirra","count":2}]},"G4677":{"id":"G4677","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4677","disambiguated_id":"G4677 =","unique_id":"G4677","headword":"Σουσάννα","transliteration":"Sousanna","lexical_morphology":"N:N-F-P","gloss_en":"Susanna","definition_en":"Σουσάννα, -ης\n (cf. Dan LXX TH Su, inscr., 2, 7, al.) \nSusanna: Luk.8:3.†\n (AS)","source_line":4824}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"Susana","count":1}]},"G4810":{"id":"G4810","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4810","disambiguated_id":"G4810 =","unique_id":"G4810","headword":"σῦκον","transliteration":"sukon","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"fig","definition_en":"σῦκον, -ου, τό \n [in LXX for תְּאֵן ] \na fig: Mat.7:16, Mrk.11:13, Luk.6:44 Jas.3:12.†\n (AS)","source_line":4958}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"figos","count":4}]},"G4956":{"id":"G4956","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4956","disambiguated_id":"G4956 =","unique_id":"G4956","headword":"συστατικός","transliteration":"sustatikos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"recommended","definition_en":"συ-στατικός (Tr. συν-), -ή, -όν \n (συνίστημι), \n__1. for putting together, constructive. \n __2. for bringing together, introductory, commendatory: ἐπιστολή (Arist., Diog. L., al.; and see MM, xxiv), 2Co.3:1.†\n (AS)","source_line":5108}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"necessitam","count":1}]},"G4983":{"id":"G4983","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4983","disambiguated_id":"G4983 =","unique_id":"G4983","headword":"σῶμα","transliteration":"sōma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"body","definition_en":"σῶμα, -τος, τό, \n [in LXX for גְּוִיָּה ,בָּשָׂר, etc., and for Aram. נְבֵלָה ;] \na body. \n__1. Prop., of the human body, \n__(a) as always in Hom. (opposite to δέμας), of the dead body: Mat.27:58, 59 Mrk.15:43, al.; \n __(b) of the living body: Luk.11:34, 1Co.6:13, al.; ἐν σ. εἶναι, Heb.13:3; as the instrument of the soul, τὰ διὰ τοῦ σ., 2Co.5:10; opposite to πνεῦμα, Rom.8:10, 1Co.5:3 7:4, Jas.2:26; to ψυχή, Mat.6:25 10:28, Luk.12:22 (cf. Wis.1:1, al.); to τὸ π. καὶ ἡ ψ., 1Th.5:23; σ. ψυχικόν, opposite to σ. πνευματικόν, 1Co.15:44; ὁ ναὸς τοῦ σ. αὐτοῦ (genitive epexeg.), Jhn.2:21; τὸ σ. τ. ταπεινώσεως (Hebraistic \"genitive of definition\"; M, Pr., 73f.; Bl., §35, 5), opposite to τὸ σ. τ. δοξῆς αὐτοῦ, Php.3:21; similarly, τὸ σ. τ. σαρκός, Col.1:22; σ. τοῦ θανάτου (subject to death), Rom.7:24; σ. τ. ἁμαρτίας, Rom.6:6; \n __(with) periphr., ἀνθρώπου, then absol., σῶμα (Soph., Xen., al.), a person, and in later writers (Polyb., al.), a slave: Rev.18:13 (cf. MM, i, ii, xxiv; Deiss., BS, 160). \n __2. Of the bodies of animals: living, Jas.3:3; dead, Heb.13:11 ( Exo.29:14, al.). \n __3. Of inanimate objects (cf. Eng. \"heavenly bodies\"): 1Co.15:37, 38 40 (Diod., al.). \n __4. Of any corporeal substance (Plat., al.): opposite to σκιά, Col.2:17. Metaphorical, of a number of persons united by a common bond; in NT, of the Church as the spiritual body of Christ: Rom.12:5, 1Co.10:16, 17 12:13, 27, Eph.1:23 2:16 4:4, 12, 16 5:23, 30, Col.1:18, 24 2:19 3:15; ἓν σ. κ. ἓν πνεῦμα, Eph.4:4. \n (AS)","source_line":5135}],"occurrence_count":142,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"corpo","count":128},{"gloss":"corpos","count":13},{"gloss":"do-corpo","count":1}]},"G502":{"id":"G502","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0502","disambiguated_id":"G0502 =","unique_id":"G0502","headword":"ἄντλημα","transliteration":"antlēma","lexical_morphology":"G:N-N","gloss_en":"bucket","definition_en":"ἄντλημα, -τος, τό\n (ἀντλέω), \n__(a) prop., what is drawn (Diosc.); \n __(b) a vessel to draw with, a bucket (Plut.; see Abbott, Essays, 88): Jhn.4:11.†\n (AS)","source_line":610}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tirar","count":1}]},"G5071":{"id":"G5071","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G5071","disambiguated_id":"G507